  "answer": "Transaction TX-0401 does not have a reason code on record. A reason code is only needed when you open a dispute, and the right one depends on what went wrong. The dispute reason codes available are:\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: you were charged more than once for the same purchase.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: a card payment online or by phone was made without your authorization.\n- **goods_not_received**: you paid, but the goods were not delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered**: you paid, but the service was not provided.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: a debit was taken from your account without your authorization.\n\nTX-0401 is a settled card payment of EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 2026-07-20. I also see TX-0402, a settled EUR 240.00 card payment to the same merchant on 2026-07-14. If you were charged twice for one purchase, **duplicate_charge** would likely apply.\n\nWhat happened with this payment? Tell me, and I can check whether a dispute is eligible under the matching code before opening anything. I won't open a dispute without your confirmation.",
